# =============================================================================
# .vercelignore — what NOT to upload when deploying.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# `vercel deploy` uploads the working directory. Without this, it would try to
# send `.toolchain/` (~500 MB of machine-local Node, pnpm and CLI binaries) and
# `node_modules/` (hundreds of MB) — a slow upload of files that Vercel either
# cannot use or will reinstall anyway.
#
# `.gitignore` is NOT consulted for this. Vercel reads `.vercelignore` for
# uploads and `.gitignore` for the Git integration; because this project deploys
# by CLI (see .github/workflows/deploy.yml), the upload list is the one that
# matters, so it is stated explicitly rather than assumed.
#
# Syntax is gitignore-like: one pattern per line, `#` comments, trailing `/` for
# directories.
# =============================================================================

# Machine-local toolchain and dependencies — 700 MB+ combined, all reproducible.
.toolchain/
node_modules/

# Build output. Vercel builds from source; uploading our local dist/ would only
# risk shipping a stale build that does not match the commit.
dist/
storybook-static/

# Local scratch.
.tmp/

# Project link state — machine-specific, and Vercel supplies its own.
.vercel/

# Local environment. .env is gitignored and may hold real credentials; it must
# never be uploaded. .env.production IS committed and is deliberately NOT
# ignored here, because the build needs its public values.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Not part of the storefront build: a DSH brand package that runs inside the
# Mitsumeru harness, with its own package.json. Uploading it changes nothing
# about the deployed site.
yammaman-brand-plugin/

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# The handoff archive, if one is sitting in the workspace.
*.zip
*.tar.gz
